{"name":"Halogen","hex":"#f4e5d2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"halogen","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any element of group 17, i.e. fluorine, chlorine, bromine, iodine, astatine and tennessine.","A light fixture in which the filament is surrounded by an atmosphere of a halogen gas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/halogen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Halogen","blocks":[{"text":"The halogens are a group in the periodic table consisting of six chemically related elements, fluorine (F), chlorine (Cl), bromine (Br), iodine (I), and the radioactive elements astatine (At) and tennessine (Ts), though some authors would exclude tennessine as its chemistry is unknown and is theoretically expected to be more like that of gallium. In the modern IUPAC nomenclature, this group is known as group 17."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Chlorine_in_bottle.jpg/330px-Chlorine_in_bottle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halogen","wikidata":"Q19605"},{"title":"Halogen (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Halogen were an Australian rock band, formed in Perth, Western Australia in 1997. Founding mainstays were Frans Bisschops on guitar and keyboards and Jasmine Yee on lead vocals – both expatriate New Zealanders. Halogen released three albums, Save the Ones You Love, Building on the Edge of the Sky and Sirens, before disbanding in 2007."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halogen_(band)","wikidata":"Q5643374"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Liquid_fluorine.jpg/330px-Liquid_fluorine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Liquid_fluorine.jpg/330px-Liquid_fluorine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F